nina: Quick heads-up — the Next.js starter that wires LangChain/LlamaIndex with our SDK has a flakey local-dev auth behavior. SSR endpoints sometimes return 401 before any client interaction. Seen this before?

omar: Is that the example that uses the dev auth proxy for ephemeral tokens?

nina: Yup. Example flow: app calls /api/session to get a short-lived cookie, then getServerSideProps fetches /api/ask which reads the cookie and calls Redwood client. In dev ~1/8 page loads the cookie is missing.

kevin: Sounds like a cookie propagation race during dev server startup. Can you paste the server handler for /api/ask?

nina: Simplified: ```js
export default async function handler(req,res){
  const token = req.cookies['redwood_token'];
  if(!token) return res.status(401).json({error:'missing token'});
  const client = new Redwood({token});
  const out = await client.complete({ prompt: req.body.prompt });
  res.json(out);
}
```

lucy: If the cookie is occasionally absent, the quick mitigation is to retry token extraction once with a tiny jitter in dev. Don't change prod semantics. Also update README Troubleshooting.

omar: Agree. Implementation guidance: wrap cookie read in a helper that, when NODE_ENV!=="production", does up to 2 immediate attempts with 30-120ms jitter. If still missing, log a debug line that suggests clearing dev cookies.

kevin: We should also add a note about App Router differences — people copy getServerSideProps patterns into app router and break token flow. Add a short example using server actions or edge functions for exchange.

nina: I'll open a small PR to: (1) add dev-only retry helper, (2) add README Troubleshooting section with one-liners (clear cookies, restart dev server), and (3) a debug log showing raw cookie header on first failure.

pr-bot: PR 2800456801 opened: fix/ssr-token-retry-dev-note — includes retry helper + README update + unit test mocking missing cookie. CI will run examples tests.

omar: Nice. For the unit test, mock the cookie store rather than using timing sleeps. Deterministic mocks reduce flakiness in CI.

kevin: Also add a tiny comment in the sample code pointing to devex doc about "SSR 401 during local dev" — saves support tickets.

lucy: One more tiny UX ask: show an example of secure server-side exchange (call auth proxy server->server) rather than using client-side token endpoints from SSR. That prevents many of these issues.

nina: Great suggestions — PR has that example and a TODO for an App Router variant. I'll merge after 1 review. Thanks! :raised_hands:
